  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]` is a site. It sequences the repository checks and holds a local `let mut errors = Vec::new()`. The requirement therefore applies to it.\n\n**Violation match.** The `fs::canonicalize(root)?` match is harmless. It runs before `errors` exists and before any check. If the root can't be resolved, every later check depends on the root, so none could run anyway. The requirement only obliges a site to run later checks that do not depend on the failed one.\n\n**Continuation after failures.** After that call, no check in the function exits early.\n- Each fallible check is turned into an `errors` entry, and the function keeps going. This covers `crate::config::load_workspace_evidence`, `crate::execution_coverage::validate_setup` and `crate::config::coverage_error`.\n- `book_source_dir` and `collect_definitions` take `&mut errors`. In `book_source_dir`, a malformed `book.toml` falls back to `md`, so definition collection and the later checks still run. Its early `return`s are inside that helper, not in the site.\n- The per-evidence-file loop pushes a \"no matching requirement or example\" error and then still calls `validate_evidence_file`. So a later check in the same iteration is not skipped.\n- The remaining steps run unconditionally in sequence: the missing-evidence check, reference discovery, `validate_committed_credentials`, `crate::sites::discover`, `validate_references`, `crate::citations::validate`, `crate::sites::validate`, `validate_cargo_examples` and `validate_rust_functions`.\n- A reference scan that fails is recorded as a discovery error and does not stop the run.\n\n**No duplicate reports.** `crate::config::coverage_error` returns `None` when the workspace file can't be read or fails the common checks. Its doc comment says those failures are already reported by `load_workspace_evidence`, so they are not reported twice. `validate_setup` locates the workspace through `Cargo.toml` and `.config/nextest.toml`, not `habeas.toml`. Its errors therefore differ from the workspace-configuration errors. The `errors` and `discovery_errors` copies serve different purposes and do not double-report one failure in the report.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[inspect_repository_with_progress]",
      "hash": "c9617bd91c99b2bd7f4138a1efb8a4a81d431c2ccf95a7701891c9a577cd8967"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/habeas-sdk/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
